  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Negative feedback"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "If temperature raises $I_C$, the drop across $R_C$ increases and $V_{CE}$ falls. Since the base is fed from the collector, $I_B = (V_{CE} - V_{BE})/R_B$ also falls, which reduces $I_C$. This automatic correction is negative feedback; it makes $S$ smaller than $1+\\beta$. A drawback is that the same feedback also reduces the ac voltage gain."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "I_C ↑ → V_CE ↓ → I_B ↓ → I_C ↓"
    },
    {
     "en": "S < 1 + β"
    },
    {
     "en": "Feedback also lowers ac gain"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "If the collector current rises, V C E falls, the base current falls, and the collector current comes back down. That is negative feedback.",
    "kn": "ಕಲೆಕ್ಟರ್ ಪ್ರವಾಹ ಏರಿದರೆ Vce ಇಳಿಯುತ್ತದೆ, ಬೇಸ್ ಪ್ರವಾಹ ಕಡಿಮೆಯಾಗುತ್ತದೆ ಮತ್ತು ಕಲೆಕ್ಟರ್ ಪ್ರವಾಹ ಮತ್ತೆ ಕಡಿಮೆಯಾಗುತ್ತದೆ. ಇದೇ ಋಣಾತ್ಮಕ ಪ್ರತಿಪೋಷಣೆ."
   }
  },
